    {tp:'rlc',q:'Find the resonant frequency, in Hz, of a series circuit with L = (1/π) H and C = (1/π) μF.',n:500,s:'√(LC) = 10⁻³/π.\nf₀ = 1/(2π√(LC)) = π/(2π × 10⁻³) = 500 Hz.'},
    {tp:'react',q:'A capacitor of (10/π) μF is connected to a 200 V (rms), 50 Hz supply. Find the rms current in mA.',n:200,s:'X(C) = 1/(2π × 50 × 10⁻⁵/π) = 1000 Ω.\nI = 200/1000 = 0.2 A = 200 mA.'},
    {tp:'power',q:'A series circuit has R = 30 Ω, X(L) = 70 Ω and X(C) = 30 Ω on a 200 V (rms) supply. Find the average power, in watts.',n:480,s:'Z = √(30² + 40²) = 50 Ω, I = 4 A.\nP = I²R = 16 × 30 = 480 W.'}
